WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.710
The Marvel Cinematic Universe's streak of
near-universally adored releases may one day

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.530
end, but not this year.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.520
Early preview audiences have taken to Twitter
in droves to rave over Spider-Man: Far From

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:18.170
Home, with many pegging it as the very best
cinematic outing for the wall-crawler so far.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.120
And considering the fact that Sony Pictures
Animation's Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.870
recently took home a Best Animated Feature
Oscar, that's really saying something.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:31.050
While there's still a moratorium on critical
reviews, this didn't stop fans who got a sneak

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:36.110
preview of the film from absolutely losing
their minds in the vaguest possible terms.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:39.750
For instance, two-time Emmy Award-winning
sports reporter Heather Catlin tweeted

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:45.239
"Far From Home is by far my favorite Spider-Man
movie. Warning, you’ll have to watch at

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:46.430
least twice."

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:50.650
We know what you're thinking: what about Sam
Raimi's Spider-Man 2, which some consider

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.680
to be among the finest superhero films ever
made? You know, that train scene is still

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.680
awesome.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:07.780
Twitter user KevinMcCarthyTV has your answer.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:13.020
"Far From Home has dethroned Sam Raimi’s
Spider-Man 2 &amp; is now [my] favorite Spider-Man

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.700
film. What’s insane is that I can’t even
tell [you] why I’m so in love with this

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.420
film because it would be a spoiler. Gyllenhaal
is incredible. Holland re-confirms as the

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.060
best Spidey to date. Amazing."

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.670
McCarthy was so excited he even had to send
a second tweet expanding on his thoughts from

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.420
the first tweet, heaping praise on director
Jon Watts.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.430
"I don’t think I’ve been this excited
to re-watch a film since Jordan Peele’s

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:41.220
Get Out &amp; Us. Watts masterfully layers incredible
action, storytelling and character development

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:46.130
into a film that will be a whole new experience
on the 2nd watch. 2 of the best end credits

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.360
scenes ever."

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.530
Geek Bomb founder Maude Garrett loved the
film's tone compared to the seriousness of

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:57.000
Avengers: Endgame, and was particularly enchanted
with Jake Gyllenhaal's Mysterio - not to mention

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.799
the post credits scenes.

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:03.290
"Spider-Man: Far From Home is SUCH a good
movie! Jake Gyllenhaal suits up &amp; completely

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:08.500
embraces his role in its entirety &amp; he’s
clearly having a blast. This is such a refreshing

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:14.290
film after the heaviness of EndGame. The post-credit
scenes are a MUST WATCH &amp; will blow your dang

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.290
mind!"

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:19.430
CNET reporter Sean Keane agreed with Garrett's
assessment of Gyllenhaal's performance, and

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.069
also reserved some praise for Zendaya as well.

00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:26.980
"Major kudos in particular to Jake Gyllenhaal
for his super engaging performance as complex

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:32.709
character Mysterio, and Zendaya, who brings
depth in her massively expanded role as MJ."

00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:33.930
"MJ, I…"

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.150
"...am Spider-Man?"

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.819
"No, of course I'm not…"

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:39.110
"I mean, it's kind of obvious."

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:43.760
Brandon Davis of ComicBook.com, meanwhile,
was just blown away by everything.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.680
"Spider-Man: Far From Home is an absolute
home run. It’s SO much fun. It’s huge

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.760
in itself and for the future of the MCU in
the most surprising ways. Tom Holland, Jake

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:59.090
Gyllenhaal, just a lethal, awesome combo!!
I cannot wait to see this movie again. And

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.160
again."

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.760
The Playlist editor-in-chief Rodrigo Perez
felt this one was even better than Spider-Man:

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:08.900
Homecoming, but warned that spoilers could
be a major problem.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:13.580
"Spider-Man: Far from Home far superior to
its predecessor &amp; really delightful, [with

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:18.930
a] terrific theme of trust well-threaded throughout.
Could say more, but it's spoiler-laden, full

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.550
of fun secrets, so be careful who you follow
and what they say.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:26.520
And finally, ultra-fan Preeti Chhibber summed
everything up, calling it the

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:32.300
"...most comic booky movie Marvel has put
out. Second and third acts are outstanding.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:36.930
The two post credit sequences are going to
stick in my brain for a L O N G time. I cannot

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.510
wait to see this movie at least three more
times. [...] My jaw dropped. And then dropped

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.659
again. It's a paradigm shift."

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:47.909
Yes, it appears that director Jon Watts, star
Tom Holland, and the rest of the crew have

00:03:47.909 --> 00:03:52.909
absolutely knocked it out of the park on this
one, and we can't say that we're surprised.

00:03:52.909 --> 00:03:56.599
After the massive success of both Captain
Marvel and Avengers: Endgame, it seems as

00:03:56.599 --> 00:04:00.379
though Marvel is poised to have its third
mega-blockbuster of the year — and we'll

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:02.950
be the first in line to hand over our money.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.900
See you there on July 2!

